<title>INDIA: India SmithKline Cons up on bonus news.</title>
<headline>India SmithKline Cons up on bonus news.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of SmithKline Beecham Consumer Healthcare Ltd surged 26.75 rupees, or 9.9 percent to 296.75 on the Bombay bourse on news the firm was meeting to decide on a bonus equity issue.  </p>
<p>The Bombay Stock Exchange said the firm's board of directors will meet later on Tuesday to consider a bonus issue of shares.</p>
<p>SmithKline shares were up 18.75 rupees, or seven percent, to 286.55 rupees on the National Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>SmithKline Beecham Consumer Healthcare is a subsidiary of SmithKline Beecham Plc of U.K. It Horlicks brand is a leader in the Indian health drinks market.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
